    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "I've called it `transformItems` for now but it doesn't seem completely accurate to me since you are actually transforming the indices config list. Maybe something like `transformIndices` or just `transform` makes more sense?\r\n\r\nThis is the standard indices config type right now but should ideally be changed to only include `indexId` and/or `indexName` (for specific ordering of indices) and `hits`. Are there other use cases for keeping `results` and `sendEvent`?",
    "commit_id": "c8a8a93c4d2fb8bba81af4cd8bea995cc8e5b9db",
    "created_at": "2026-01-07T15:37:56Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -133,6 +137,21 @@ export type AutocompleteProps<TItem extends BaseHit> = ComponentProps<'div'> & {\n       };\n   getSearchPageURL?: (nextUiState: IndexUiState) => string;\n   onSelect?: AutocompleteIndexConfig<TItem>['onSelect'];\n+  transformItems?: (\n+    indices: Array<{\n+      indexName: string;\n+      indexId: string;\n+      hits: Hit[];\n+      results: SearchResults;\n+      sendEvent: SendEventForHits;\n+    }>\n+  ) => Array<{\n+    indexName: string;\n+    indexId: string;\n+    hits: Hit[];\n+    results: SearchResults;\n+    sendEvent: SendEventForHits;\n+  }>;",
